  "id": "COMPOUND:17935 - PROTEIN:3514",
  "verbalization": "Protobioside appears to have a shared target, Peptide deformylase, through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Protobioside acts as a target of Digoxigenin and 8-Prenylluteone, both of which in turn target Peptide deformylase. This indicates a potential regulatory or enzymatic relationship where Protobioside may influence the activity of these compounds, which then interact with Peptide deformylase. The presence of multiple indirect links implies that Protobioside may exert a modulatory effect on the pathway leading to Peptide deformylase, possibly through a mechanism involving the activation or inhibition of the intermediaries. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Protobioside in the regulation of Peptide deformylase, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
